# Class: resource:CHEMINF_000191 (ionization energy descriptor)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 resource:CHEMINF_000191 "An ionization energy descriptor is a descriptor that describes the minimum amount of energy required to remove an electron (to an infinite distance) from an atom or molecule in a gaseous state.

X + energy → X+ + e-

The term 'ionization potential' has historically been used but is now no longer recommended. ")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 resource:CHEMINF_000191 "ionization energy")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 resource:CHEMINF_000191 "ionization enthalpy")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 resource:CHEMINF_000191 "ionization potential")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label resource:CHEMINF_000191 "ionization energy descriptor"@en)
SubClassOf(resource:CHEMINF_000191 resource:CHEMINF_000094)

