# Class: resource:CHEMINF_001542 (hybridization ratio)

AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description resource:CHEMINF_001542 "Characterizes molecular complexity in terms of carbon hybridization states.")
AnnotationAssertion(cheminf:short_name resource:CHEMINF_001542 "hybratio")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment resource:CHEMINF_001542 "It reports the fraction of sp3 carbons to sp2 carbons as Nsp3/ (Nsp3 + Nsp2). The original form of the descriptor (i.e., simple ratio) has been used to characterize molecular complexity, especially in the are of natural products , which usually have a high value of the sp3 to sp2 ratio. Other short names: HybridizationRatio, HybRatio.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label resource:CHEMINF_001542 "hybridization ratio"@en)
SubClassOf(resource:CHEMINF_001542 resource:CHEMINF_000092)

# Class: resource:CHEMINF_001543 (Kier and Hall kappa molecular shape indices)

AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description resource:CHEMINF_001543 "Descriptor that calculates Kier and Hall kappa molecular shape indices.")
AnnotationAssertion(cheminf:short_name resource:CHEMINF_001543 "kierValues")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment resource:CHEMINF_001543 "Kier and Hall kappa molecular shape indices compare the molecular graph with minimal and maximal molecular graphs. First kappa shape index is given by n ( n - 1 ) 2 m 2 , second kappa shape index is given by ( n - 1 ) ( n - 2 ) 2 p 2 2 and third kappa shape index is given by ( n - 1 ) ( n - 3 ) 2 p 3 2 for odd n and ( n - 3 ) ( n - 2 ) 2 p 3 2 for enev n, where n denotes the number of atoms in the hydrogen suppressed graph, m is the number of bonds in the hydrogen suppressed graph. Also, let p2 denote the number of paths of length 2 and let p3 denote the number of paths of length 3. Other short names: KappaShapeIndices, Kier1, Kier2, Kier3.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label resource:CHEMINF_001543 "Kier and Hall kappa molecular shape indices"@en)
SubClassOf(resource:CHEMINF_001543 resource:CHEMINF_000092)

# Class: resource:CHEMINF_001544 (partial pi charge)

